  "//devDependencies-testing-library-dom": "@testing-library/dom is pinned so @testing-library/react and @testing-library/user-event share one installed copy; a second copy re-splits user-event's act()-aware config and every user-event interaction dispatches outside act() with no test failing. Do not remove or loosen this pin without running `npm run check:dom-dedupe` first. See #219 (the original defect), #224 (the guard), and #313 (the guard runs in the test-build CI job, so loosening this pin without a shared version fails CI, not just the manual check).",
  "devDependencies": {
    "@babel/parser": "8.0.4",
    "@playwright/test": "^1.62.1",
    "@testing-library/dom": "^10.4.1",
    "@testing-library/jest-dom": "^7.0.1",
    "@testing-library/react": "^16.3.3",
    "@testing-library/user-event": "^14.6.6",
    "axios-mock-adapter": "^2.1.0",
    "jest-util": "^30.4.1",
    "nodemon": "^3.1.9",
    "postcss": "8.5.26",
    "react-scripts": "^5.0.1",
    "redux-mock-store": "^1.5.5",
    "source-map-explorer": "^2.5.3",
    "supertest": "^7.2.2",
    "yaml": "^2.9.0"
  },
  "//eslintConfig-jest-scoping": "react-app/jest declares the testing-library rules in an override whose globs are unanchored ('**/*.{spec,test}.*'), so extending it at the top level applied React/DOM testing rules to server/test/*.test.js, which run under node --test with no DOM. It is scoped to client test globs here instead. Keep this an allowlist: scope the preset, never disable its rules under server/**, or each rule the preset adds later leaks back until someone extends an off-list. Keep the globs extension-agnostic ('*' and '.*'), exactly as the preset writes them: ESLint derives which extensions to lint in a directory from the overrides patterns, so spelling them out as '.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}' silently pulls .jsx/.ts/.tsx client tests into `eslint src server` for the first time (528 files -> 636, surfacing 161 pre-existing errors). Anchoring to src/ is the whole change. Do not edit this block without running `npm run test:eslint-scoping` after; the `guards` job now runs the unified lint (`npm run lint`, #284/#659), so a scoping regression that widens the surface also surfaces there. See #207.",
  "eslintConfig": {
    "extends": [
      "react-app"
    ],
    "overrides": [
      {
        "files": [
          "src/**/__tests__/**/*",
          "src/**/*.{spec,test}.*"
        ],
        "extends": [
          "react-app/jest"
        ]
      },
      {
        "files": [
          "server/**/*.js",
          "scripts/**/*.js"
        ],
        "excludedFiles": [
          "scripts/k6-*.js"
        ],
        "env": {
          "node": true
        },
        "parserOptions": {
          "sourceType": "script"
        },
        "rules": {
          "strict": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "files": [
          "scripts/k6-*.js"
        ],
        "globals": {
          "__ENV": "readonly",
          "__ITER": "readonly",
          "__VU": "readonly"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "browserslist": {
    "production": [
      ">0.2%",
      "not dead",
      "not ie <= 11",
      "not op_mini all"
    ],
    "development": [
      "last 1 chrome version",
      "last 1 firefox version",
      "last 1 safari version"
    ]
  },
  "jest": {
    "testMatch": [
      "**/src/**/__tests__/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}",
      "**/src/**/*.{spec,test}.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}"
    ]
  }
}
